b-a755-0d996363fe0f" :question/math-academy-id "q-149742" :question/problem "Find the value of the double sum\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{8}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{11}{a}_{i}({b}_{j}-6)\n$$\n\ngiven that\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{8}{a}_{i}=15,\\,{\\sum }_{j=1}^{11}{b}_{j}=68.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The product rule for double summations states that\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{a}_{i}{b}_{j}={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{a}_{i}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{b}_{j}.\n$$\n\nSo, using the product rule for double summations, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{8}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{11}{a}_{i}({b}_{j}-6) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{8}{a}_{i}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{11}({b}_{j}-6).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the rules for single summations, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{8}{a}_{i}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{11}({b}_{j}-6) & =({\\sum }_{i=1}^{8}{a}_{i})\\cdot ({\\sum }_{j=1}^{11}{b}_{j}-{\\sum }_{j=1}^{11}6) \\\\  & =({\\sum }_{i=1}^{8}{a}_{i})\\cdot ({\\sum }_{j=1}^{11}{b}_{j}-6{\\sum }_{j=1}^{11}1) \\\\  & =(15)\\cdot (68-6\\cdot 11) \\\\  & =(15)\\cdot (68-66) \\\\  & =(15)\\cdot (2) \\\\  & =30\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-149742/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "08375770-c610-5dae-b01b-c457de086cba"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-149742"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-149736/selection/9d283c5011602849ca0ed985c78c31f0123564be0c231e9425e42f5854955bfd" :answer/id #uuid "a4fffd85-7b5a-5872-8a69-91e62aa52bf0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "355" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-149736/selection/8c8bb55dda8210bf85ea7035316340e0c7ca9e0efa59bc03f9ebb06571047294" :answer/id #uuid "c79714c0-634d-56f8-b317-4ff6f523c7b9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "353" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-149736/selection/21c8f9501c831bcb93fff63d4bd87307ef09e12ccaa742070a1e4fb360642ae5" :answer/id #uuid "94ec8758-a34c-547a-8bce-755804178aa7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "325" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-149736/selection/8363b4f5b6aa50ec876c28f20d0454d5e28a9856e5d5553bbaf60e87edf3d608" :answer/id #uuid "3aba4c03-2240-57cd-b904-eab60d584d8b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "352" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-149736/selection/4cd7e68ca4dc7a3ea725571a6860c3e1e4090ced7cff84ef33c048f865979a66" :answer/id #uuid "aac5a646-8fbc-50d2-a52b-4f31207ba7f0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "335" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-149736/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "4b4b8a93-fb1b-55c8-9887-1e0897c985c6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-149736/selection/21c8f9501c831bcb93fff63d4bd87307ef09e12ccaa742070a1e4fb360642ae5" :answer-field/choices ["q-149736/selection/9d283c5011602849ca0ed985c78c31f0123564be0c231e9425e42f5854955bfd" "q-149736/selection/8c8bb55dda8210bf85ea7035316340e0c7ca9e0efa59bc03f9ebb06571047294" "q-149736/selection/21c8f9501c831bcb93fff63d4bd87307ef09e12ccaa742070a1e4fb360642ae5" "q-149736/selection/8363b4f5b6aa50ec876c28f20d0454d5e28a9856e5d5553bbaf60e87edf3d608" "q-149736/selection/4cd7e68ca4dc7a3ea725571a6860c3e1e4090ced7cff84ef33c048f865979a66"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-149736" :question/id #uuid "4825646e-446d-5585-9d07-aa29f475bcaa" :question/math-academy-id "q-149736" :question/problem "Find the value of the double sum\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{15}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{15}({a}_{i}-2)({b}_{j}+3)\n$$\n\ngiven that\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{15}{a}_{i}=35,\\,{\\sum }_{j=1}^{15}{b}_{j}=20.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The product rule for double summations states that\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{a}_{i}{b}_{j}={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{a}_{i}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{b}_{j}.\n$$\n\nSo, using the product rule for double summations, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{15}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{15}({a}_{i}-2)({b}_{j}+3) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{15}({a}_{i}-2){\\sum }_{j=1}^{15}({b}_{j}+3).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the rules for single summations, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{15}({a}_{i}-2){\\sum }_{j=1}^{15}({b}_{j}+3) & =({\\sum }_{i=1}^{15}{a}_{i}-{\\sum }_{i=1}^{15}2)\\cdot ({\\sum }_{j=1}^{15}{b}_{j}+{\\sum }_{j=1}^{15}3) \\\\  & =({\\sum }_{i=1}^{15}{a}_{i}-2{\\sum }_{i=1}^{15}1)\\cdot ({\\sum }_{j=1}^{15}{b}_{j}+3{\\sum }_{j=1}^{15}1) \\\\  & =(35-2\\cdot 15)\\cdot (20+3\\cdot 15) \\\\  & =(35-30)\\cdot (20+45) \\\\  & =(5)\\cdot (65) \\\\  & =325.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-149736/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "08375770-c610-5dae-b01b-c457de086cba"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-149736"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-6116"] :question/problem "Evaluate $\\displaystyle \\sum_{j=1}^3\\sum_{i=1}^2 (i+j).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we write out the inner summation by summing over the index $i\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{3}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{2}(i+j) & ={\\sum }_{j=1}^{3}[{\\sum }_{i=1}^{2}(i+j)] \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{j=1}^{3}[(1+j)+(2+j)] \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{j=1}^{3}(3+2j)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we calculate the sum above by summing over the index $j\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{3}(3+2j) & =(3+2\\cdot 1)+(3+2\\cdot 2)+(3+2\\cdot 3) \\\\  & =5+7+9 \\\\  & =21\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-6118"] :question/problem "Find the value of the double sum\n\n$$\n\\sum_{i=1}^{5} \\sum_{j=1}^{8} (1+2a_{ij}-b_{ij})\n$$\n\ngiven that\n\n$$\n\\sum_{i=1}^{5} \\sum_{j=1}^{8}  a_{ij} = 8, \\qquad\\sum_{i=1}^{5} \\sum_{j=1}^{8}  b_{ij} = 15.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The sum and constant multiple rules for double summations state that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({a}_{ij}+{b}_{ij}) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{a}_{ij}+{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{b}_{ij}, \\\\ {\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}k{a}_{ij} & =k{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{a}_{ij}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the sum rule to the given double summation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{5}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{8}(1+2{a}_{ij}-{b}_{ij}) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{5}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{8}1+{\\sum }_{i=1}^{5}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{8}2{a}_{ij}-{\\sum }_{i=1}^{5}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{8}{b}_{ij} \\\\  & =({\\sum }_{i=1}^{5}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{8}1)+2{\\sum }_{i=1}^{5}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{8}{a}_{ij}-{\\sum }_{i=1}^{5}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{8}{b}_{ij} \\\\  & =({\\sum }_{i=1}^{5}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{8}1)+2(8)-15 \\\\  & =({\\sum }_{i=1}^{5}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{8}1)+1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the fact that\n\n$$\n\\sum_{i=1}^m\\sum_{j=1}^n 1 = mn,\n$$\n\nwe have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({\\sum }_{i=1}^{5}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{8}1)+1 & =5\\cdot 8+1 \\\\  & =40+1 \\\\  & =41.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\sum_{i=1}^{5} \\sum_{j=1}^{8} (1+2a_{ij}-b_{ij}) = 41.\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-10521"] :question/problem "Find the value of the double sum\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle \\sum_{i=1}^{15} \\sum_{j=1}^{18} (a_{i} - 2)( b_{j}+1)\n$$\n\ngiven that\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle \\sum_{i=1}^{15}a_i = 40, \\qquad \\displaystyle \\sum_{j=1}^{18}b_j =-8 .\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The product rule for double summations states that\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle\\sum_{i=1}^m\\sum_{j=1}^n  a_{i}b_j = \\sum_{i=1}^m a_i \\sum_{j=1}^n b_{j}.\n$$\n\nSo, using the product rule for double summations, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{15}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{18}({a}_{i}-2)({b}_{j}+1) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{15}({a}_{i}-2){\\sum }_{j=1}^{18}({b}_{j}+1).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the rules for single summations, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{15}({a}_{i}-2){\\sum }_{j=1}^{18}({b}_{j}+1) & =({\\sum }_{i=1}^{15}{a}_{i}-{\\sum }_{i=1}^{15}2)\\cdot ({\\sum }_{j=1}^{18}{b}_{j}+{\\sum }_{j=1}^{18}1) \\\\  & =({\\sum }_{i=1}^{15}{a}_{i}-2{\\sum }_{i=1}^{15}1)\\cdot ({\\sum }_{j=1}^{18}{b}_{j}+{\\sum }_{j=1}^{18}1) \\\\  & =(40-2\\cdot 15)\\cdot (-8+18) \\\\  & =(10)\\cdot (10) \\\\  & =100.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
